    {
      "block_id": "h2-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Preflight",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `scripts/rig_relay_test_duplicate_audit.py`: ruff clean, pyright clean - Audit runs: 5970 tests scanned, max-exact-duplicate-groups=1 passes",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Audit Inspection Findings",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The 35 normalized AST groups are mostly **false positives** from over-aggressive normalization. The normalizer strips model/variable names, so per-model validation tests (`test_rejects_unknown_fields` on `DecisionReason` vs `BlockedIntent` vs `AllowedIntent`) appear identical. These are legitimate separate tests — each model needs its own validation.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The 618 assert-shape groups are statistical clusters (largest: 479 members across 142 files). Not actionable without per-class analysis.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Groups Parametrized",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "test_governance_engine.py — TestGovernanceEngine",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**Before**: 20 individual test methods, each calling `GovernanceEngine.evaluate_action_legality()` with hardcoded parameters and asserting a specific decision or reason code.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**After**: 2 parametrized contract matrices + 4 remaining distinct tests = 20 cases:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-12",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Matrix",
        "Cases",
        "Parametrized IDs"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Decision outcome",
          "11",
          "`allowed_read_only_intent`, `blocked_provider_trust_tier`, `blocked_provider_unavailable`, `blocked_provider_error`, `not_blocked_unavailable_read_only`, `requires_review_mutation`, `allows_mutation_when_allow_mutation`, `requires_review_network`, `allows_network_when_allow_network`, `blocked_dirty_policy`, `not_applicable_no_capabilities`"
        ],
        [
          "Reason codes",
          "5",
          "`reason_provider_trust_tier_blocked`, `reason_mutation_requires_review`, `reason_network_requires_review`, `reason_dirty_policy_violated`, `reason_no_requested_capabilities`"
        ],
        [
          "Remaining",
          "4",
          "`test_allowed_read_only_includes_allowed_intent`, `test_blocked_intent_includes_reason_code`, `test_blocked_when_multiple_checks_fail`, `test_pure_no_side_effects`"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**Failure diagnostics preserved**: Each parametrized case has a human-readable ID. When a test fails, the node ID (e.g., `test_evaluate_action_legality_decision[blocked_provider_trust_tier]`) immediately identifies the scenario.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
